# The link to beehive over the network (Docs/beehive-network-plan.html): a
# machine without the AI serial port pairs with beehive and gets the same
# ask / explain / wish as over the serial port. beehive runs on the host with
# its fake backend and one paired machine.
@net
@ai-net
$ net dhcp
~ 10\.0\.2\.15
$ ai
AI features: on
bridge:      none (no COM2 port in this machine; over the network: ai connect HOST NAME KEY)
$ ask hello
~ no AI bridge

# A wrong key: beehive stays silent, and `ai` says why there is no link.
$ ai connect {hive} {hive-name} abcde-fghij-kmnpq-rstuv
~ ^connecting to beehive as machine 'test'
~ ^not encrypted
~ ^not connected: refused: wrong key or name
$ ai
~ ^bridge:      network, as machine 'test': not connected: refused: wrong key or name
$ ask hello
~ offline|not connected

# The right key.
$ ai connect {hive} {hive-name} {hive-key}
connected (fake fake)
~ ^\[hive\] connected to beehive over the network$
$ ai
~ ^bridge:      network, as machine 'test': beehive online \(fake fake\) for .*, not encrypted$
$ ask what is this
BeeHive fake backend (no LLM).
Question: what is this
$ wish a banner from the network
Thanks! Saved to /system/inbox/signals.jsonl and sent to the AI host.
$ nosuchcommand
$ explain
~ nosuchcommand

# Ctrl+C stops a long answer; the link stays.
$^C ask slow please
$ ask again
Question: again

# The kill switch closes the connection, and keeps it closed.
$ ai off
AI features switched off.
$ ai
AI features: off ('ai on' to enable)
~ not connected: AI features are switched off
$ ask hello
~ switched off
$ ai on
$ ai
~ beehive online
$ ask back again
Question: back again

# The key is never shown, and the event log has no address.
$ ai
!~ {hive-key}
$ log 40
!~ 10\.0\.2\.2
~ hive

# Malformed settings are refused.
$ ai connect {hive} {hive-name} not-a-key
~ not a pairing key
$ ai connect {hive} Bad_Name {hive-key}
~ ^usage: ai connect
$ ai connect
~ ^usage: ai connect

$ ai disconnect
network link to beehive removed, and its key with it
$ ai
bridge:      none (no COM2 port in this machine; over the network: ai connect HOST NAME KEY)
@signal "target": "test", "kind": "wish", "text": "a banner from the network"
